# Z Home Interiors — Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development. On Vercel (or any
# other host), set these under Project Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# This project currently ships with NO required environment variables — it
# is fully static and has no backend, database, or third-party API calls.
# The variables below are either recommended for correct deployment
# behavior, or forward-looking placeholders for integrations mentioned in
# docs/GOOGLE_SETUP.md that are not yet wired into the code.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# RECOMMENDED — affects correctness of canonical URLs, Open Graph tags,
# and the generated sitemap (app/sitemap.ts, lib/seo.ts).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# The fully-qualified, no-trailing-slash URL this deployment is served from.
# - Production:  https://www.zhomeinteriors.com
# - Staging:     https://staging.zhomeinteriors.com
# - Vercel preview builds: your preview URL, e.g. https://z-home-interiors-git-branch.vercel.app
#
# If unset, the app falls back to the hardcoded production URL in
# config/site.ts — meaning a preview/staging deployment would incorrectly
# emit production URLs in its metadata and sitemap. Always set this outside
# of local development.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.zhomeinteriors.com

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORWARD-LOOKING — not yet read by any code in this repo. Add the
# corresponding integration (see docs/GOOGLE_SETUP.md) before setting these,
# or they'll have no effect.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Google Analytics 4 Measurement ID (e.g. G-XXXXXXXXXX).
# Wire this into app/layout.tsx (e.g. via @next/third-parties/google's
# <GoogleAnalytics /> component) when analytics is implemented.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# Google Site Verification meta tag content, from Search Console's
# "HTML tag" verification method. Wire into app/layout.tsx's
# `metadata.verification.google` field when verifying the property.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONTACT FORM — required for the contact form to actually send email.
# Without these three set, app/api/contact/route.ts returns a clear
# "not configured" response and the form tells the visitor to call or
# WhatsApp instead — it never pretends to have sent a message it didn't.
#
# Set these as real secrets in your hosting provider's dashboard (e.g.
# Vercel Project Settings → Environment Variables). Never commit real
# values to the repository. The default provider wired into
# app/api/contact/route.ts is Resend (https://resend.com) — swap the
# fetch call in that file if you use a different provider.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Resend API key.
# EMAIL_API_KEY=

# The inbox that should receive contact form enquiries.
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=hello@zhomeinteriors.in

# The "from" address — must be a domain verified with your email provider.
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=enquiries@zhomeinteriors.in
